<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTATION</div><h1>Project information</h1><p>Overview of the Network Equipment Inventory System.</p></div></div>
<section class="panel about-panel"><div class="about-hero"><div class="brand-mark large">NI</div><div><div class="eyebrow">SCHOOL PROJECT / ORGANIZATIONAL USE</div><h2>Network Equipment Inventory System</h2><p>A web-based application for maintaining a centralized record of network equipment in an organization.</p></div></div>
<div class="about-grid"><div><h3>Problem addressed</h3><p>Organizations may track routers, switches, access points, firewalls, cabling and related assets using paper records or scattered spreadsheets. This can make it difficult to find equipment, identify its location, review its condition and plan maintenance.</p></div><div><h3>Proposed solution</h3><p>The system centralizes asset details in a searchable register, tracks status and condition, stores maintenance history and produces an exportable inventory report.</p></div><div><h3>Core objectives</h3><ul><li>Maintain accurate equipment records.</li><li>Locate assets by tag, IP address, category or location.</li><li>Track equipment status, condition and warranty dates.</li><li>Record repairs and scheduled maintenance.</li><li>Generate inventory summaries and CSV exports.</li></ul></div><div><h3>Technology stack</h3><ul><li>Frontend: HTML, CSS and JavaScript</li><li>Backend: PHP</li><li>Database: SQLite (local file database)</li><li>Runtime: UwAmp Apache on Windows</li></ul></div></div>
<div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon">!</span><div><b>Before organizational deployment</b><p>This edition is suitable for a local demonstration and project evaluation. Set a strong administrator password locally, back up the database regularly, restrict access to trusted users, and test on a separate copy before entering production data. Role-based access is provided for administrators, technicians and viewers. Administrators manage accounts and assets; technicians update assigned equipment and log maintenance; viewers have read-only access.</p></div></div></section>
